8. Sort the People – LeetCode
Problem
Sort people's names according to their heights in descending order.
Java Solution
import java.util.*;
 
class Solution {
 
   public String[] sortPeople(String[] names, int[] heights) {
 
       Integer[] index = new Integer[names.length];
 
       for (int i = 0; i < names.length; i++) {
           index[i] = i;
       }
 
       Arrays.sort(index, (a, b) ->
           Integer.compare(heights[b], heights[a])
       );
 
       String[] result = new String[names.length];
 
       for (int i = 0; i < names.length; i++) {
           result[i] = names[index[i]];
       }
 
       return result;
   }
}
Example
Input:
 
names = ["Mary","John","Emma"]
heights = [180,165,170]
 
Output:
 
["Mary","Emma","John"]
Explanation
Heights:
Mary  → 180
Emma  → 170
John  → 165
So the descending order is:
Mary → Emma → John
 
